        "original_id": "8e72a1a3-0e18-5773-a01e-6b42ea7cf3ba",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Old Fashioned, gin and tonic\n- Organizations: Pendennis Club\n- Concepts: cocktails, highball cocktails, garnish\n\nFacts:\n- Sometime in the 1880s, the Pendennis Club was the birthplace by name, not invention, of the Old Fashioned.\n- The Pendennis Club may have given the name to what was possibly the first mixed drink to be called a cocktail.\n- The Old Fashioned is a cocktail made by muddling sugar with bitters, then adding alcohol such as whiskey or brandy and a twist of citrus rind.\n- A gin and tonic is a highball cocktail made with gin and tonic water poured over ice.\n- A gin and tonic is usually garnished with a slice or wedge of lime.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "feea3937-9e83-5ae5-9b82-cc2f2044011b",
        "text": "Page: Old Fashioned. Sentence: The Old Fashioned is a cocktail made by muddling sugar with bitters, then adding alcohol, such as whiskey or brandy, and a twist of citrus rind.\nPage: Gin and tonic. Sentence: A gin and tonic is a highball cocktail made with gin and tonic water poured over ice.\nPage: Gin and tonic. Sentence: It is usually garnished with a slice or wedge of lime.\nPage: Pendennis Club. Sentence: Sometime in the 1880s, the club was the birthplace (by name, not invention) of the Old Fashioned, possibly the first mixed drink to be called a cocktail.",
